{"ts": "2026-11-03T19:04:06.290029Z", "run_id": "r-20261103T1902Z-8312", "unit": "openspec:add-dbos-runtime", "seq": 5, "type": "human.verdict", "question": "Q-020", "target": "F-da2b0827", "decision": "accept", "by": "delegate", "reason": "The finding repeats F-233c28d7, which Q-018 waived for the same unchanged code, and the repository supports that waiver. The adapter does forward String(entry) for every level with { component: \"dbos\" }, and only replaces a lowercase pg-style \"error: ...\" tail with \"error: [redacted]\". The same scenario in spec.md line 19 requires that after pg_terminate_backend no log line holds \"terminating connection\", the frozen launch test asserts exactly that, and design decision 2 and security point 4 say DBOS and pg error text is never copied because it can hold a URL. DBOS writes its own system-database client errors through this adapter, so forwarding the text unchanged would violate those clauses; confining redaction to the pool-error path, as the judge suggests, would not cover DBOS's own lines. The literal \"String(entry)\" wording conflicts with the stricter clauses and Q-018 already recorded that a follow-up amends the spec text; the code is not what needs to change.", "text_sha256": "17a0bee8308cc0b4089dce7268944d402f91a4efca88402d1e2b0eebcb8b2d8b", "answer_sha256": "230f21f34445303f3d530738cb7e4431bcdb02a7ed2f89f23d48a1255ea6bf0a", "profile": "delegate-fable", "model": "claude-fable-5-1", "cli": "claude-code"}
